`form-program-image-bmf-subset-lower.fk` accepts an explicit bounded grammar value and typed result templates. Before any IR escapes it validates:

- exact spec, rule, limits, byte-class and template shapes;
- integer-only positive limits beneath compiler-owned ceilings;
- unique and resolved rules/classes, an existing start rule and acyclic references;
- only `lit`, variable `seq`, ordered `alt`, `ref`, and `cap(run)` patterns;
- canonical byte ranges and `cap(run)` class resolution;
- per-rule definite captures, including intersection across alternatives;
- exact pattern/literal/capture/result and emitted row/string/function bounds.

The lowerer derives variable image-local function, node and string definitions from the data, including distinct entry and start roots, and sends them through the unchanged symbolic linker. Query-sequence and allow/deny-choice grammars produce different linked topology; a same-topology literal mutation changes the IR with no Form definition change. Exact replay recomputes both IR and linked numeric streams. Duplicate/unresolved/cyclic/unsupported/over-bound inputs and forged spec/IR wrappers refuse with IR=`nothing`.

